  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 245 AM EDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nOver the course of the long term, mid-level ridging set up across \nthe Desert Southwest will gradually translate eastward -- supporting \na transition from northwesterly flow to something more nearly weak \nand quasi-zonal. In the absence of stronger kinematics, any \ndisturbances traversing mid-upper flow may help to locally bolster \nconvective coverage (or perhaps intensity) but by and large, \nscattered to numerous garden variety summertime thunderstorms are \nexpected each afternoon through the extended range. \n\nMoisture streaming off of the Gulf will support dewpoints in the mid-\nto-upper 70s and PWATs generally 1.7\" or higher. Abundant moisture \ncombined with seasonable afternoon highs (in the upper 80s to 90s) \nwill support a return to heat index values in the triple digits. \nHeat Advisory criteria is likely to be met for at least subsets of \nthe eastern portion of the area, and subsequent product issuance is \npossible assuming trends continue. Conversely, the aforementioned \nconditions set the stage for continued chances for locally heavy \nrainfall in any storms that form, along with isolated flash flooding \nconcerns.",
